00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:24,457
Then it's settled.

262
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:27,577
Let's find an island with
a doctor on it right away.

263
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:30,917
First things first, we need to
hurry and get Nami healthy again.

264
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,397
Then we head for Alabasta.

265
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,337
After all, we need her at the
helm to move at top speed.

266
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:36,250
Right?

267
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:38,860
No one makes this ship move like Nami.

268
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,680
Princess, hold on.

269
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:44,897
Won't finding a doctor for Nami take time
the citizens of Alabasta just don't have?

270
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:45,810
That's right.

271
00:14:45,893 --> 00:14:49,277
So the sooner we get Nami a doctor,
the sooner we can get to Alabasta.

272
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,200
Those are wise words, Vivi.

273
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,184
You're beautiful and brilliant.

274
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:54,660
The girl's got guts.

275
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:56,760
Thank you, Vivi.

276
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,024
Don't overexert yourself, Nami.

277
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,550
I'm...

278
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:05,463
I'm sorry.

279
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:08,520
I may need to, like... Nami!

280
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,840
What the hell is that?!

281
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,540
It's a cyclone!

282
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:14,640
It's huge!

283
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,190
Wait!

284
00:15:16,273 --> 00:15:18,494
That's the same path we were headed on!

285
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:19,497
Phoebe's right!

286
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:21,317
That's the exact same direction!

287
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,457
It would've been a direct hit
if we kept going straight!

288
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:24,893
We'd be dead right now!

289
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,520
See that?

290
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:35,780
Way too close!

291
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,220
We barely missed it!

292
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:39,390
Incredible.

293
00:15:39,473 --> 00:15:42,237
Cyclones in the Grand Line are
said to be impossible to predict.

294
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,880
But somehow Nami did.

295
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,477
However she does it,

296
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:48,497
it's obvious her technique isn't
based on any conventional method.

297
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:51,437
It's as if she's detecting
the weather with her body.

298
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:54,120
It's beyond reason. A miracle.

299
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:55,830
Alright!

300
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:57,686
What are we waiting here for?

301
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:59,720
Let's find Nami a doctor!

302
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,350
Yeah!

303
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,860
Oh, what are we going to do, Vivi?

304
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,620
Nami's fever won't go down!

305
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:25,840
Hey, guys, stop!

306
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,767
That behavior isn't helping!

307
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,460
See any doctors yet?

308
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:37,428
Lupi, you can't be serious.

309
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:44,037
Uh hey guys what do you think about people

310
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:47,017
standing on water what
do i think it's possible?

311
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:49,697
What kind of question
is that it's impossible

312
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:54,617
of course yeah well then
what's that what's what?

313
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:55,940
Say what?

314
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:19,680
Hello, sure it's chilly today.

315
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,140
Yeah, it is chilly today.

316
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,857
Definitely, it's very chilling.

317
00:17:24,940 --> 00:17:27,293
In fact, I would even say it's freezing.

318
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,430
Really?

319
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,240
Increase buoyancy! Right!

320
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:43,600
What is that thing? A watermelon?

321
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:45,260
Why are we shaking?

322
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,817
Hold the rudder steady!

323
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:50,900
If anything happens to Nami, I'll
hold every one of you responsible!

324
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:55,360
What the hell is that?

325
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,900
Is that a ship?

326
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,040
Oh, crap!

327
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,200
It's a pirate ship!

328
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,200
It's huge!

329
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:25,870
Great.

330
00:18:25,953 --> 00:18:27,406
Just when we needed to hurry.

331
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:31,160
What's the matter?

332
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:35,618
Don't tell me our underwater raid
ship, the Tin Tyrant, surprised you!

333
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:43,340
Phoebe, you're in charge. All right.

334
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:46,120
Hey, what's going on?

335
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,640
So, what's going on?

336
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:05,904
Well, we're under attack
and it's still snowing.

337
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:13,197
Well yeah the guns pointing
at my face kind of gave

338
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:19,057
that one away what next you
all consider Yourself a band

339
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:20,857
of pirates that's amusing

340
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:26,777
i only count for you sort

341
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:30,580
of strange that your group
would have so few members.

342
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:36,820
Kid, it's just weird.

343
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:39,560
What kind of guy likes to eat knives? Ah!

344
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,239
My gums are bleeding just watching!

345
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:45,880
All right, I'll keep this simple.

346
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:49,900
See, my men here and I wish
to travel to Drum Kingdom.

347
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:54,239
You wouldn't happen to have an
eternal pose or a Log Pose, would you?

348
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:55,680
Nope, can't help.

349
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:59,136
Sorry, but I've never even
heard of this Drum Kingdom.

350
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:03,477
Well, now that we have that all settled,
would you guys just leave already?

351
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:06,157
We're in a hurry, and we don't
have time to deal with all this.

352
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:09,057
You'll never enjoy life if
you're always in a rush.

353
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:11,837
But if you have neither
pose, what can be done?

354
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:15,508
I suppose I'll have to settle
for your treasure on this ship.

355
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:16,760
First things first.

356
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:19,340
I'm feeling a bit hungry.

357
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:26,277
He's a shippity monster!

358
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:29,140
Hey, our ship isn't your lunch! Be quiet!

359
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:31,437
Wapol doesn't like to be
disturbed while he's eating!

360
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:32,350
Shut up!

361
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:34,437
Damn pirate, we're under attack!

362
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:35,350
Shoot him!

363
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:39,280
Now things are finally
starting to get interesting.

364
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:40,690
Perfect.

365
00:20:40,773 --> 00:20:42,637
This is more like it. Stop it!

366
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,014
Can't we discuss this?

367
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:53,040
They took it upon themselves
to start this. What fools!

368
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,614
They got a death wish?

369
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:56,230
Gunfire!

370
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:58,157
Karoo, stay here and watch Nami.

371
00:20:58,240 --> 00:20:59,358
I'll be right back.

372
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,064
You shouldn't take on
anything you can't handle.

373
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,310
Reception!

374
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,220
Oh, Bart, no bite.

375
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,900
Hey, um, Wapol, we need help.

376
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:36,980
You still eat it!

377
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:39,820
This ship doesn't taste
half bad. Hey, you!

378
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:41,380
You fool!

379
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:42,677
You're no master Wapol.

380
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:45,397
Now you'll be eaten by the
power of the Munch Munch.

381
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:46,520
Let me know!

382
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:49,470
What's this?

383
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,160
Oh, hey there, Vivi.

384
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:53,149
Everything okay with Nami?

385
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:58,920
I'd prefer someone less chewy.

386
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:02,620
I said...

387
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:11,430
Waffle?

388
00:22:13,780 --> 00:22:14,880
This is bad.

389
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,317
He sent Waffle flying out into the ocean.

390
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:19,640
Bad? It's worse. It's a disaster.

391
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:20,797
Waffle's gonna drown.

392
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:21,710
He can't swim.

393
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:22,960
Recall the troops.

394
00:22:23,180 --> 00:22:24,457
There's no time to waste.

395
00:22:24,540 --> 00:22:27,437
We have to rescue him before
he sinks to the bottom!

396
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,420
Go, go, go!

397
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:31,140
This is far from over! You'll pay!

398
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:32,535
I promise you'll pay!

399
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:34,500
You're dead, you brat!

400
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:37,080
You'd better hope Waffle doesn't die!

401
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:39,104
Or it's your blood we'll spill!

402
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:40,240
Remember that!

403
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:41,920
We'll get you for this!

404
00:22:45,640 --> 00:22:46,680
Wow, crazy.

405
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:48,627
Those guys are really upset.

406
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:51,517
What were they calling that
old garbage can, Waffle?

407
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:53,457
Who cares about what his name was?

408
00:22:53,540 --> 00:22:54,775
Don't worry about it.

409
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,740
The guy's obviously a moron.

410
00:22:56,860 --> 00:22:58,625
Best to just forget about him.

411
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:06,617
I know him.

412
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:07,920
But from where?

413
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:19,220
I know.

414
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:20,837
Dows her in water.

415
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:21,977
That'll fix her.

416
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:22,980
You idiot!

417
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:25,120
This isn't good.

418
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:28,057
The sun's about to set
and she's still the same.

419
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:28,970
Yeah, right.

420
00:23:29,053 --> 00:23:31,317
Maybe it would be best if
we drop anchor somewhere.

421
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:35,037
We can't navigate at night anyway
without the help of Nami's instructions.

422
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:35,950
That's true.

423
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:07,380
It sure is a cold one.

424
00:24:11,140 --> 00:24:12,560
Almost a full moon.

425
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:29,260
Crap, I fell asleep.

426
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:32,380
You're up early.

427
00:24:32,980 --> 00:24:34,957
Can't just sit around doing nothing.

428
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:38,628
We've got to find a way out of
this jam as quick as possible.

429
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:39,650
You're right.

430
00:24:39,900 --> 00:24:41,080
That's a good point.

431
00:24:48,080 --> 00:24:52,917
Say, Usa, does this area
seem unusually calm and cold?

432
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,588
Yeah, now that you
mention it, it sure does.

433
00:24:55,740 --> 00:24:58,034
And to be honest, it's freaking me out.

434
00:24:58,660 --> 00:25:00,837
The Grand Line just
keeps getting stranger.

435
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:02,567
That's not necessarily true.

436
00:25:03,140 --> 00:25:03,970
Huh?

437
00:25:04,053 --> 00:25:05,664
Maybe there's an island nearby.

438
00:25:06,060 --> 00:25:09,257
Hey, Sanji, will you check the
horizon for any sign of land?

439
00:25:09,340 --> 00:25:10,170
Sure thing.

440
00:25:11,140 --> 00:25:14,081
There's a Winter Island
somewhere nearby, I think.

441
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:15,050
Winter Island?

442
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,497
Scattered within the Grand Line,

443
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:21,677
there are four basic types of islands
made distinct by their varying climates.

444
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:24,231
You've got Summer Islands, Spring Islands,

445
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:27,367
Autumn Islands, and of
course Winter Islands.

446
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:30,426
Each one has its own
four independent seasons.

447
00:25:30,620 --> 00:25:32,177
When traveling on the Grand Line,

448
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:33,877
there are at least 16 different types of

449
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:36,517
weather patterns you must
be prepared to endure,

450
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,297
ranging from Summer Island, Summer,

451
00:25:38,380 --> 00:25:41,457
all the way to Winter Island,
Winter, and everything in between.

452
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,577
There can always be exceptions to this,

453
00:25:43,660 --> 00:25:46,577
and you could even encounter unknown
climates at any given moment.

454
00:25:46,660 --> 00:25:47,880
I think I get it.

455
00:25:48,460 --> 00:25:52,037
The Grand Line has all these different
islands, one after the other.

456
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,117
And that's the reason why the seas between

457
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:57,500
them have such crazy unstable
weather patterns. Correct.

458
00:25:57,860 --> 00:26:01,357
And the closer you get to an island,
the calmer the sea is around you.

459
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:04,558
Which is why I asked Sanji
to start looking for land.

460
00:26:05,060 --> 00:26:05,890
That's it.

461
00:26:05,973 --> 00:26:06,803
I see it.

462
00:26:07,260 --> 00:26:08,090
Huh?

463
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:11,760
Island dead ahead!

464
00:26:14,020 --> 00:26:15,220
Are you serious?

465
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:16,700
Oh, an island!

466
00:26:16,840 --> 00:26:17,797
We found an island!

467
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:19,337
Hey, Nami, did you hear that?

468
00:26:19,420 --> 00:26:21,357
This means we can get
you to a real doctor.

469
00:26:21,440 --> 00:26:23,060
He'll fix you up. Wake up.

470
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:29,500
Wake up.

471
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:30,997
Wake up. Wake up.

472
00:26:31,080 --> 00:26:31,910
Wake up.

473
00:26:31,993 --> 00:26:32,823
Just go, Luke.

474
00:26:32,906 --> 00:26:33,736
I've got her covered.

475
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:38,900
There it is!

476
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:40,000
Nami's saved!

477
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:42,700
All right, it's snow.

478
00:26:42,960 --> 00:26:45,100
A snow island. Whoa.

479
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:46,500
Luffy, wait.

480
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:49,217
Just so there's no
misunderstanding between us.

481
00:26:49,300 --> 00:26:51,476
We're stopping to find Nami a doctor.

482
00:26:51,600 --> 00:26:53,617
We're not here to have an adventure.

483
00:26:53,700 --> 00:26:55,000
Are we clear?

484
00:26:56,660 --> 00:26:58,097
I love snow.

485
00:26:58,180 --> 00:27:01,260
It's so white. It's no use. He's gone.

486
00:27:02,380 --> 00:27:03,240
Hold on.

487
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:04,877
You sure this is a good idea?

488
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:06,377
There could be snow monsters.

489
00:27:06,460 --> 00:27:09,197
Besides, we don't even know if
there's people there or not.

490
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:10,110
Oh, no.

491
00:27:10,193 --> 00:27:12,117
I'm having a relapse if I
don't go to the island disease.

492
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:13,360
Ah, snow.

493
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:15,460
It's so white and beautiful.

494
00:27:16,240 --> 00:27:18,593
Guess I'll get ready for the inevitable.

495
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:48,257
Ah, I'm so happy!

496
00:27:48,340 --> 00:27:49,680
Look at the snow!

497
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,557
Look at the mountains.

498
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:53,934
They're unlike anything I've ever seen.

499
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:57,360
Say, Luffy, aren't you
cold dressed like that?

500
00:27:57,600 --> 00:28:00,012
It's ten degrees below freezing out here.

501
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:02,532
That's when bears get ready to hibernate.

502
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:05,350
Huh?

503
00:28:05,433 --> 00:28:06,520
Oh, boy. Cold!

504
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,209
You just figured that out!

505
00:28:13,180 --> 00:28:15,140
It's a stream of melted snow.

506
00:28:15,380 --> 00:28:17,851
This may provide a good spot to disembark.

507
00:28:18,360 --> 00:28:19,940
Okay guys, Dr.

508
00:28:20,120 --> 00:28:21,355
Search, who wants in?

509
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:23,437
Guess we gotta find people here first.

510
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:24,920
I'm in! Me too!

511
00:28:25,340 --> 00:28:26,660
Ah, go have fun!

512
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:28,640
That's far enough, pirates!

513
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:44,870
People!

514
00:28:44,953 --> 00:28:46,036
Well, that was easy.

515
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:47,470
Yeah, nice.

516
00:28:47,553 --> 00:28:49,261
But they don't seem too friendly.

517
00:28:50,620 --> 00:28:52,300
I'll only say this once.

518
00:28:52,780 --> 00:28:54,960
Your kind is not welcome here.

519
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:56,379
Leave immediately.

520
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:58,800
We only came here to find a doctor.

521
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:00,537
We have someone who's sick.

522
00:29:00,620 --> 00:29:02,077
You'll have to do better than that.

523
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:03,857
We won't fight for that old trip.

524
00:29:03,940 --> 00:29:05,220
This is our island.

525
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:08,097
We won't let any filthy pirates land here.

526
00:29:08,180 --> 00:29:12,840
Raise anchor and leave now or we'll
blow you and your ship out of the water.

527
00:29:13,140 --> 00:29:17,900
That's great We barely said
hello, and they already hate us?

528
00:29:20,680 --> 00:29:21,560
Big mistake!
